{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf7J7nCTiod1B8oGjBDo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GmpVDExWW6MWA6j7GtbBuL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/dl_eng/h && sed -n 270,335p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-260; grep -n \"^- \\`game.settings\\|settings.glyphs\\|menu: {\\|game.menu(\" API-INDEX.md | head; grep -n \"input: {\\|custom.*actions\\|bindings\" AI_GUIDE.md | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8184,"cache_read_input_tokens":68589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8184,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9b39171-d84f-4593-93cb-80dd0e6441b3","uuid":"fd4dd174-5dd6-47dd-9365-d908beb03a16","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:15:04.060Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf7J7PPm9eZDnDHjeUJE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GmpVDExWW6MWA6j7GtbBuL":{"command":"cd /tmp/dl_eng/h && sed -n 270,335p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-260; grep -n \"^- \\`game.settings\\|settings.glyphs\\|menu: {\\|game.menu(\" API-INDEX.md | head; grep -n \"input: {\\|custom.*actions\\|bindings\" AI_GUIDE.md | head"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GmpVDExWW6MWA6j7GtbBuL","type":"tool_result","content":"- `new E.Input(screen, map, signal) → input`: signal: an AbortSignal that removes every listener this adds (game.dispose()). A screen without a canvas (headless) gets no DOM listeners: input comes from press(code), release(code), tap(action) and hold(action, o\n- `E.Input.DEFAULT { attack, dash, skill, jump }`: top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks\n- `E.Input.PLATFORMER { jump, attack, dash, skill }`: side-scrollers (Mario, Mega Man): Space / Z / K jump, X / J attack or shoot, Shift / C dash\n- `E.Input.SHMUP { fire, bomb }`: shoot-'em-ups (1942, Gradius): Space / Z / J fire (hold for autofire), X / K bomb\n- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C crouch (a toggle), E interact, J attack, K \n- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1,\n- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n- `input.bindButtons(root)` †: wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action\n- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long press, then a dr\n- `input.buffered(a, win = .15)`: was it pressed within the last `win` seconds and not yet consumed? (input buffering)\n- `input.clear()`: Release all devices and discard buffered input on focus loss or a modal transition.\n- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD \n- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n- `input.doubleTap()` †: [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null\n- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n- `input.drag()` †: how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) instead of by the stick's direction\n- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long pr\n- `input.history` †: the last second of input, oldest first: [{ t (input.clock), dir (numpad 1-9 for a fighter facing right: 5 neutral), pressed: the actions pressed then, directions aside }], one entry each time the direction changes or a button is pressed: a\n- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n- `input.longPress()` †: [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null\n- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forward, forward, attack: a fireball); '623' a\n- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n- `input.pan()` †: [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button; else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free)\n- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Returns null when done, the action that already uses the code (\n- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } \n- `input.release(code)`: let go of a code pressed with press()\n- `input.released(a)`: true only during the first update step after the action was let go\n- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n- `input.resetBindings()` †: forget the player's bindings: every action back to its preset's codes\n- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n- `input.screenPoint(cx, cy)` †: browser client coords -> screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space, with no camera), or null without a canvas\n- `input.sequence(steps, o = {})` †: true on the step a sequence of inputs ends, each one after the last within window seconds (.5) of the first: input.sequence(['down', 'down+right', 'right', 'attack']). A step names actions joined by +: its directions are he\n- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n- `input.suppress(a)` †: Suppress a held action until the next tick (a HUD widget owns the pointer this step).\n- `input.suppressCode(code)` †: A widget owns this button; other devices bound to the same action still work.\n- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n- `input.tick(dt)`: advance input by one step: read the gamepad and turn presses since the last step into this step's pressed() and released() (the engine calls it every step)\n- `input.touchArea()` †: where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or null while none show: keep a prompt or a box clear of it (a bottom E.Dialog does by itself)\n- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size them): input.touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'], { labels: { jump:\n- `input.touchSet(a, label = null, show = true)` †: one touch button as the moment changes: its label (TALK beside someone, NEXT in a dialog; null: its own) and whether it shows (false: nothing for it to do here). Cheap to call every step: input.touchSet('conf\n- `input.unbind(a, device)` †: take away action a's codes for one device ('keys' or 'pad'); the arrow keys and d-pad stay on the moves\n- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, THIRDPERSON, SHMUP\n- `input.zoom()` †: the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. The game applies it (game.zoomBy)\n- `input.zoomPoint()` †: [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle)\n- `input.aimSource = 'move'` †: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad'\n- `input.clock = 0`: seconds of input time (the steps' dt added up)\n- `input.deadzone = .18`: how far a gamepad stick moves before it counts (0..0.8)\n- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n- `input.held`: the key and button codes down right now ('KeyD', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump')\n- `input.keysTo = null` †: the other players' inputs the keyboard's codes go to as well (players sharing it, each with half its keys: game.players)\n- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n- `input.map`: each action's codes ({ jump: ['Space', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump'] }); every action also answers to 'Act:<name>' (DOM buttons with data-act, tap, hold)\n- `input.mouse`: { cx, cy } its page position, active once it has moved over the canvas, t the input clock when it last moved\n- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n- `input.pad = 'any'` †: the gamepad this input reads: 'any' (the first connected one another player hasn't: player 1's), an index (a joined player's own), or null (none)\n- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181340__x96eb17/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9b39171-d84f-4593-93cb-80dd0e6441b3","uuid":"70d89824-d4cd-4b14-879a-6c68424ab1f5","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:15:04.085Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `new E.Input(screen, map, signal) → input`: signal: an AbortSignal that removes every listener this adds (game.dispose()). A screen without a canvas (headless) gets no DOM listeners: input comes from press(code), release(code), tap(action) and hold(action, o\n- `E.Input.DEFAULT { attack, dash, skill, jump }`: top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks\n- `E.Input.PLATFORMER { jump, attack, dash, skill }`: side-scrollers (Mario, Mega Man): Space / Z / K jump, X / J attack or shoot, Shift / C dash\n- `E.Input.SHMUP { fire, bomb }`: shoot-'em-ups (1942, Gradius): Space / Z / J fire (hold for autofire), X / K bomb\n- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C crouch (a toggle), E interact, J attack, K \n- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1,\n- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n- `input.bindButtons(root)` †: wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action\n- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long press, then a dr\n- `input.buffered(a, win = .15)`: was it pressed within the last `win` seconds and not yet consumed? (input buffering)\n- `input.clear()`: Release all devices and discard buffered input on focus loss or a modal transition.\n- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD \n- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n- `input.doubleTap()` †: [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null\n- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n- `input.drag()` †: how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) instead of by the stick's direction\n- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long pr\n- `input.history` †: the last second of input, oldest first: [{ t (input.clock), dir (numpad 1-9 for a fighter facing right: 5 neutral), pressed: the actions pressed then, directions aside }], one entry each time the direction changes or a button is pressed: a\n- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n- `input.longPress()` †: [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null\n- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forward, forward, attack: a fireball); '623' a\n- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n- `input.pan()` †: [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button; else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free)\n- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Returns null when done, the action that already uses the code (\n- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } \n- `input.release(code)`: let go of a code pressed with press()\n- `input.released(a)`: true only during the first update step after the action was let go\n- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n- `inp