{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf7qT7fMo8gRHTTUd3QB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JitRf7FbKw8xvo6QKtUbec","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/dl_eng/h && grep -n \"^- \\`game.go\\|^- \\`new E.Combo\\|^- \\`combo\\.\\|^- \\`new E.Attack\\|^- \\`attack\\.\\|^- \\`r.marker\\|^- \\`r.prop\\|^- \\`r.textAt\\|^- \\`new E.Bullets\\|^- \\`shots\\.\\|^- \\`new E.FlowField\\|^- \\`flow\\.\\|^- \\`game.hitFx\\|^- \\`game.script\\|^- \\`E.until\\|^- \\`new E.Body\\|^- \\`body\\.\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-330"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12764,"cache_read_input_tokens":133529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12764,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9b39171-d84f-4593-93cb-80dd0e6441b3","uuid":"74a7eae0-947b-4e5f-891b-76144bc23207","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:22:19.869Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf7qSmKYYbuzaGQ3e1rz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JitRf7FbKw8xvo6QKtUbec":{"command":"cd /tmp/dl_eng/h && grep -n \"^- \\`game.go\\|^- \\`new E.Combo\\|^- \\`combo\\.\\|^- \\`new E.Attack\\|^- \\`attack\\.\\|^- \\`r.marker\\|^- \\`r.prop\\|^- \\`r.textAt\\|^- \\`new E.Bullets\\|^- \\`shots\\.\\|^- \\`new E.FlowField\\|^- \\`flow\\.\\|^- \\`game.hitFx\\|^- \\`game.script\\|^- \\`E.until\\|^- \\`new E.Body\\|^- \\`body\\.\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-330"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JitRf7FbKw8xvo6QKtUbec","type":"tool_result","content":"424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a stat\n436:- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris', 'mosaic', 'swirl' or 'dissolve', each way taking opts.seconds (.4), round opts.\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a number (seconds), nothing (one step), a condition (a function, or E.until(fn)), a \n599:- `E.until(fn)` †: a script's wait until fn() is true: yield E.until(() => door.open)\n640:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n653:- `new E.Combo(specs, o = {}) → combo`: new E.Combo(items, { window: .3 }): items are move names, specs or Attacks\n654:- `combo.active`: true while the current hit can connect\n655:- `combo.busy`: true while a hit of the chain is swinging\n656:- `combo.cancel()`: stop the chain; the next press starts it over\n657:- `combo.current`: the Attack of the current hit\n658:- `combo.hits(targets, test, fn)`: the current hit's hits(targets, test, fn): fn(target) once per swing where test(target) is true\n659:- `combo.press()`: start or continue the chain. Returns true if a hit started\n660:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n661:- `combo.update(dt)`: advance the current hit; returns the phase that began, as Attack.update\n662:- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n663:- `combo.moves`: the Attacks\n664:- `combo.step = -1`: the index of the current hit (-1 before the first)\n665:- `combo.window`: seconds after a hit ends that a press still chains\n817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus \n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n821:- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jum\n822:- `flow.update(x, y)`: aim the field at a world point; it rebuilds only when the target's cell or the map (map.version) changes\n823:- `flow.climb`: how much higher a next-door top may be (an agent that climbs walls)\n824:- `flow.d`: each cell's distance in steps to the target cell (1e9 where it can't get there), row by row\n825:- `flow.drop`: how much lower (an agent that hops down)\n826:- `flow.jump` †: the widest gap jumped (world units, 0 = none)\n827:- `flow.jumpDrop`, `flow.jumpRise` †: how much higher and lower a jump may land\n828:- `flow.map`: the map it paths over\n829:- `flow.step`: the height difference walked over freely (2)\n830:- `flow.tx = -1`, `flow.ty = -1`: the target's cell\n831:- `flow.version = -1`: the map's version it was built for\n921:- `new E.Body(o = {}) → body`: new E.Body({ x, y, r: 5, ... })\n922:- `body.jump(v = 220)`: leave the ground with upward speed v (only when standing). Returns true if it jumped\n923:- `body.push(ix, iy, iz = 0)`: add an impulse (knockback, explosion): push(vx, vy, vz)\n924:- `body.update(dt, map)`: move it one step: speed, friction, walls (map.collide: lower walls are walked onto), gravity and the ground under it (map.groundAt)\n925:- `body.bounce = 0`: 0..1, how much speed it keeps off walls and the floor\n926:- `body.bounced = false`: it hit the ground and bounced up this step (dust, a thud)\n927:- `body.friction = 0`: slows vx and vy per second (0 = none)\n928:- `body.gravity = 700`: pulls z down (world units per second squared)\n929:- `body.groundZ = 0`: the height of what is under it\n930:- `body.h = 32` †: its height (32, a standing actor's: it spans z to z + h, so it passes under a solid shape above that and walks into one in that span)\n931:- `body.hitWall = false`: it touched a wall this step\n932:- `body.landed = false`: it landed this step\n933:- `body.onGround = true`: standing\n934:- `body.r = 5`: its radius\n935:- `body.step = 2`: the height it walks up without jumping (E.HEIGHTS.step)\n936:- `body.vx = 0`, `body.vy = 0`, `body.vz = 0`: its speed, world units per second\n937:- `body.x = 0`, `body.y = 0`, `body.z = 0`: its position (z = feet)\n1019:- `new E.Bullets(game, o = {}) → shots`: new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side', max: 800, sparks: true }); game: its game\n1020:- `shots.burst(base, vels)`: fire several at once from a pattern list of [vx, v2] (v2 = vy on the ground plane, vz in side view)\n1021:- `shots.clear(team)`: remove every bullet, or only one team's\n1022:- `shots.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (glowing cores, or their sprites)\n1023:- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n1024:- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits\n1025:- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n1026:- `shots.list = []`: the live bullets\n1027:- `shots.max`: at most this many at once\n1028:- `shots.plane`: 'ground' (they fly over x and y) or 'side' (x and z)\n1029:- `shots.sparks`: a puff of sparks where one hits a wall\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181340__x96eb17/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9b39171-d84f-4593-93cb-80dd0e6441b3","uuid":"4f53cd7b-b22b-4fe2-9fe7-cd777b869b8e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:22:19.888Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an