{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9gZ2arRSouEoAQH56r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011CafjKGG3VHreA1sDqQLic","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181340__x96eb17/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, re\nsrc = {\n \"date\":\"2026-11-02 18:13\",\n \"source\":\"The Sopranos (1999-2007), HBO. An original spiritual successor with parody names and no copied text or art.\",\n \"genre\":\"Action-adventure with beat-em-up brawling, shakedown dialogue choices and a stress-and-diet survival layer\",\n \"perspective\":\"Three-quarter view by default (the engine's native view); the player can switch to top-down or isometric and zoom\",\n \"tech\":\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (single-file JS engine, canvas 2D, no other libraries); hand-written JS modules bundled into one HTML file; AI Hub session client 1.3.0\",\n \"artDirection\":\"Engine-native procedural pixel puppets (HD Humanoid rigs and Blobs) on lit TileMap levels at a 400x225 base resolution, with weather, lights and drawn controller glyphs\",\n \"animation\":\"Engine-native skeleton rigs: E.Humanoid moves (jab, cross, hook, haymaker, sweep), poses, expressions, Combo/Attack timing, tweens and scripts\",\n \"audio\":\"Code-written chip music (title, town, fight, therapy, woods, diner, boss), code-written sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish blips for every voice\",\n \"online\":\"AI Hub session protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: each copy plays the same seeded Main Street round and sees the others as ghosts. No other networking.\",\n \"testing\":\"Efficient, lightweight testing: headless Chromium smoke runs, an attract-mode autopilot playing the whole episode, keyboard and fake-gamepad checks, the AI Hub harness (2 and 4 players, host-leave) and a 13-viewport WebKit matrix. No real iOS Safari or physical DualSense.\",\n \"research\":\"None online beyond the engine handoff and AI Hub docs; the Sopranos tone is from memory.\",\n \"environment\":\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n \"model\":\"Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n \"usage\":\"Session time about 35 minutes (18:13 to about 18:48). Cost and token counts: unknown.\"\n}\ntf=[\"About 9 real issues: the attract autopilot's scene changes dropped the demo flag, it snagged on NPCs and lamp posts, it stopped short of exit zones, the woods objective pointed at an unreachable waypoint, a 'move' action warning, em dashes that the font cannot draw, and overlapping HUD, boss-bar and results text. A stale web server also gave a false hub-harness failure.\",\n\"Two were game-breaking for the flow (the woods and yard soft-locks of the attract tour); none crashed, and no JS errors appeared in any run.\",\n\"Running the attract-mode autopilot through the whole episode while polling game state and taking screenshots: it exercised dialogue, combat, scene changes, saves and the ending in one go.\",\n\"The viewport matrix overflow check: it reported all 13 viewports clean, but a full-screen canvas game cannot overflow, so only its screenshots helped. Also my first long run piped through tail, which showed nothing until it finished.\"]\nef=[\"The rigs and lighting give a lot of look for free, and the standard features (pause, settings, controls rebinding, save slots) plus Dialog with live portraits, Combo/Attack and FlowField saved a great deal of work.\",\n\"Yes: input.label has no 'move' action, FlowField ignores prop colliders so the autopilot walked into NPCs, game.go clears state so every scene change had to carry the demo flag, and I guessed a 'ring' prop that does not exist.\",\n\"The game layer: enemy AI, the stress/gut/respect systems, shakedown and therapy scripts, the attract autopilot, AI Hub ghost sync, furniture boxes, and drawn PlayStation/Xbox glyphs (the engine font has no controller symbols).\",\n\"Confirming exact method semantics without reading the engine source, such as what combo.hits expects, overlay coordinates, and how scene changes interact with game state.\",\n\"I would overhaul how area changes work: re-entering the whole scene through game.go, which clears timers and particles, is awkward for rooms within one game.\",\n\"Add first-class solid props and NPC colliders shared by Body and FlowField, and controller glyph shapes in the font.\"]\npf=[\"The clear definition of done and fixed deliverables, the 10-foot controller-first philosophy, the inverted-stick toggle as a realistic constraint, and the instruction to pick the title with a real random generator.\",\n\"Whether the single-file rule and 'dependencies need not be included' conflict, how the bracketed file name should be formatted, what 'root' means, and how a hub round with no title screen fits the standalone title and attract mode.\",\n\"Scope: a complete vertical slice with attract mode, hub ghost play, controller glyphs, saves, a story in the source's tone and only code-written assets.\",\n\"A deterministic full-episode bot test asserting chapter progression, which I approximated with the attract autopilot, plus a run on a real DualSense.\"]\nd={\"sourceInformation\":src,\"testingFeedback\":tf,\"engineFeedback\":ef,\"promptFeedback\":pf,\n\"aiHub\":{\"name\":\"The Soprano Diet\",\"tagline\":\"Ducks. Doctors. Deli meat.\",\"description\":\"A Jersey mob boss tries to survive a day of shakedowns, rival crews, therapy and a dream in the snow while his cardiologist watches his plate. Brawl, bargain and keep your stress down.\",\"type\":\"Game\",\"genre\":\"Action\",\"source\":\"The Sopranos (1999-2007)\",\"series\":\"The Sopranos\",\"players\":\"1–4\",\"controls\":\"Move: left stick/WASD. Punch: Square/J/click. Dodge: Circle/Space. Interact: Cross/E. The Look: Triangle/Q. Eat: L1/R. Camera: R3/V.\",\"tags\":[\"story\",\"comedy\",\"pixel art\",\"retro\",\"boss fights\",\"top-down\"]}}\njson.dump(d,open('exit-interview.json','w'),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.load(open('exit-interview.json')); print('json ok')\n# about text\na=open('TheSopranoDiet-TheSopranos-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-181340/src/09a-about.js').read()\ndef L(x): return json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False)\nlines=[\"Date: \"+src['date'],\"Source: \"+src['source'],\"Genre and Perspective: \"+src['genre']+\". \"+src['perspective']+\".\",\"Tech: \"+src['tech'],\"Art Direction: \"+src['artDirection'],\"Animation: \"+src['animation'],\"Audio: \"+src['audio'],\"Online: \"+src['online'],\"Testing: \"+src['testing'],\"Research: \"+src['research'],\"Environment: \"+src['environment'],\"Model: \"+src['model'],\"Usage: \"+src['usage']]\ndef sec(h,items): return \"  { h: %s, lines: %s }\"%(L(h),L(items))\nout=\"/* About / credits text: the in-game copy of Source Information and the feedback sections */\\nSD.ABOUT = [\\n\"+\",\\n\".join([sec('SOURCE INFORMATION',lines),sec('TESTING FEEDBACK',tf),sec('ENGINE FEEDBACK',ef),sec('PROMPT FEEDBACK',pf),sec('CREDITS',[\"Design, code, music and writing: Claude (claude-sonnet-5-5). Engine: my-3D2dge by Michael Crosato. Hub protocol: AI Hub. The Sopranos belongs to its creators; this is a parody and a fan letter.\"])])+\"\\n];\\n\"\nopen('TheSopranoDiet-TheSopranos-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-181340/src/09a-about.js','w').write(out)\nEOF\nnode TheSopranoDiet-*/build.mjs | tail -1; cd /tmp/sdtest && python3 smoke.py 2>&1 | tail -3; grep -ci \"todo\\|placeholder\\|stub\" /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/*x96eb17/work/TheSopranoDiet-*/src/*.js | grep -v \":0\"; ls /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/*x96eb17/work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":504,"cache_read_input_tokens":293060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":504,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9b39171-d84f-4593-93cb-80dd0e6441b3","uuid":"1f997d79-0c78-41e2-a488-518cec2874fb","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:46:38.797Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9gYYomnowF9JiTo1Kj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011CafjKGG3VHreA1sDqQLic":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181340__x96eb17/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, re\nsrc = {\n \"date\":\"2026-11-02 18:13\",\n \"source\":\"The Sopranos (1999-2007), HBO. An original spiritual successor with parody names and no copied text or art.\",\n \"genre\":\"Action-adventure with beat-em-up brawling, shakedown dialogue choices and a stress-and-diet survival layer\",\n \"perspective\":\"Three-quarter view by default (the engine's native view); the player can switch to top-down or isometric and zoom\",\n \"tech\":\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (single-file JS engine, canvas 2D, no other libraries); hand-written JS modules bundled into one HTML file; AI Hub session client 1.3.0\",\n \"artDirection\":\"Engine-native procedural pixel puppets (HD Humanoid rigs and Blobs) on lit TileMap levels at a 400x225 base resolution, with weather, lights and drawn controller glyphs\",\n \"animation\":\"Engine-native skeleton rigs: E.Humanoid moves (jab, cross, hook, haymaker, sweep), poses, expressions, Combo/Attack timing, tweens and scripts\",\n \"audio\":\"Code-written chip music (title, town, fight, therapy, woods, diner, boss), code-written sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish blips for every voice\",\n \"online\":\"AI Hub session protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: each copy plays the same seeded Main Street round and sees the others as ghosts. No other networking.\",\n \"testing\":\"Efficient, lightweight testing: headless Chromium smoke runs, an attract-mode autopilot playing the whole episode, keyboard and fake-gamepad checks, the AI Hub harness (2 and 4 players, host-leave) and a 13-viewport WebKit matrix. No real iOS Safari or physical DualSense.\",\n \"research\":\"None online beyond the engine handoff and AI Hub docs; the Sopranos tone is from memory.\",\n \"environment\":\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n \"model\":\"Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n \"usage\":\"Session time about 35 minutes (18:13 to about 18:48). Cost and token counts: unknown.\"\n}\ntf=[\"About 9 real issues: the attract autopilot's scene changes dropped the demo flag, it snagged on NPCs and lamp posts, it stopped short of exit zones, the woods objective pointed at an unreachable waypoint, a 'move' action warning, em dashes that the font cannot draw, and overlapping HUD, boss-bar and results text. A stale web server also gave a false hub-harness failure.\",\n\"Two were game-breaking for the flow (the woods and yard soft-locks of the attract tour); none crashed, and no JS errors appeared in any run.\",\n\"Running the attract-mode autopilot through the whole episode while polling game state and taking screenshots: it exercised dialogue, combat, scene changes, saves and the ending in one go.\",\n\"The viewport matrix overflow check: it reported all 13 viewports clean, but a full-screen canvas game cannot overflow, so only its screenshots helped. Also my first long run piped through tail, which showed nothing until it finished.\"]\nef=[\"The rigs and lighting give a lot of look for free, and the standard features (pause, settings, controls rebinding, save slots) plus Dialog with live portraits, Combo/Attack and FlowField saved a great deal of work.\",\n\"Yes: input.label has no 'move' action, FlowField ignores prop colliders so the autopilot walked into NPCs, game.go clears state so every scene change had to carry the demo flag, and I guessed a 'ring' prop that does not exist.\",\n\"The game layer: enemy AI, the stress/gut/respect systems, shakedown and therapy scripts, the attract autopilot, AI Hub ghost sync, furniture boxes, and drawn PlayStation/Xbox glyphs (the engine font has no controller symbols).\",\n\"Confirming exact method semantics without reading the engine source, such as what combo.hits expects, overlay coordinates, and how scene changes interact with game state.\",\n\"I would overhaul how area changes work: re-entering the whole scene through game.go, which clears timers and particles, is awkward for rooms within one game.\",\n\"Add first-class solid props and NPC colliders shared by Body and FlowField, and controller glyph shapes in the font.\"]\npf=[\"The clear definition of done and fixed deliverables, the 10-foot controller-first philosophy, the inverted-stick toggle as a realistic constraint, and the instruction to pick the title with a real random generator.\",\n\"Whether the single-file rule and 'dependencies need not be included' conflict, how the bracketed file name should be formatted, what 'root' means, and how a hub round with no title screen fits the standalone title and attract mode.\",\n\"Scope: a complete vertical slice with attract mode, hub ghost play, controller glyphs, saves, a story in the source's tone and only code-written assets.\",\n\"A deterministic full-episode bot test asserting chapter progression, which I approximated with the attract autopilot, plus a run on a real DualSense.\"]\nd={\"sourceInformation\":src,\"testingFeedback\":tf,\"engineFeedback\":ef,\"promptFeedback\":pf,\n\"aiHub\":{\"name\":\"The Soprano Diet\",\"tagline\":\"Ducks. Doctors. Deli meat.\",\"description\":\"A Jersey mob boss tries to survive a day of shakedowns, rival crews, therapy and a dream in the snow while his cardiologist watches his plate. Brawl, bargain and keep your stress down.\",\"type\":\"Game\",\"genre\":\"Action\",\"source\":\"The Sopranos (1999-2007)\",\"series\":\"The Sopranos\",\"players\":\"1\\u20134\",\"controls\":\"Move: left stick/WASD. Punch: Square/J/click. Dodge: Circle/Space. Interact: Cross/E. The Look: Triangle/Q. Eat: L1/R. Camera: R3/V.\",\"tags\":[\"story\",\"comedy\",\"pixel art\",\"retro\",\"boss fights\",\"top-down\"]}}\njson.dump(d,open('exit-interview.json','w'),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.load(open('exit-interview.json')); print('json ok')\n# about text\na=open('TheSopranoDiet-TheSopranos-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-181340/src/09a-about.js').read()\ndef L(x): return json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False)\nlines=[\"Date: \"+src['date'],\"Source: \"+src['source'],\"Genre and Perspective: \"+src['genre']+\". \"+src['perspective']+\".\",\"Tech: \"+src['tech'],\"Art Direction: \"+src['artDirection'],\"Animation: \"+src['animation'],\"Audio: \"+src['audio'],\"Online: \"+src['online'],\"Testing: \"+src['testing'],\"Research: \"+src['research'],\"Environment: \"+src['environment'],\"Model: \"+src['model'],\"Usage: \"+src['usage']]\ndef sec(h,items): return \"  { h: %s, lines: %s }\"%(L(h),L(items))\nout=\"/* About / credits text: the in-game copy of Source Information and the feedback sections */\\nSD.ABOUT = [\\n\"+\",\\n\".join([sec('SOURCE INFORMATION',lines),sec('TESTING FEEDBACK',tf),sec('ENGINE FEEDBACK',ef),sec('PROMPT FEEDBACK',pf),sec('CREDITS',[\"Design, code, music and writing: Claude (claude-sonnet-5-5). Engine: my-3D2dge by Michael Crosato. Hub protocol: AI Hub. The Sopranos belongs to its creators; this is a parody and a fan letter.\"])])+\"\\n];\\n\"\nopen('TheSopranoDiet-TheSopranos-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-181340/src/09a-about.js','w').write(out)\nEOF\nnode TheSopranoDiet-*/build.mjs | tail -1; cd /tmp/sdtest && python3 smoke.py 2>&1 | tail -3; grep -ci \"todo\\|placeholder\\|stub\" /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/*x96eb17/work/TheSopranoDiet-*/src/*.js | grep -v \":0\"; ls /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/*x96eb17/work"}}}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"bfq2fhce4","run_id":"0mw011nwe-eb8bd522","tool_use_id":"toolu_011CafjKGG3VHreA1sDqQLic","description":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181340__x96eb17/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, re\nsrc = {\n \"date\":\"2026-11-02 18:13\",\n \"source\":\"The Sopranos (1999-2007), HBO. An original spiritual successor with parody names and no copied text or art.\",\n \"genre\":\"Action-adventure with beat-em-up brawling, shakedown dialogue choices and a stress-and-diet survival layer\",\n \"perspective\":\"Three-quarter view by default (the engine's native view); the player can switch to top-down or isometric and zoom\",\n \"tech\":\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (single-file JS engine, canvas 2D, no other libraries); hand-written JS modules bundled into one HTML file; AI Hub session client 1.3.0\",\n \"artDirection\":\"Engine-native procedural pixel puppets (HD Humanoid rigs and Blobs) on lit TileMap levels at a 400x225 base resolution, with weather, lights and drawn controller glyphs\",\n \"animation\":\"Engine-native skeleton rigs: E.Humanoid moves (jab, cross, hook, haymaker, sweep), poses, expressions, Combo/Attack timing, tweens and scripts\",\n \"audio\":\"Code-written chip music (title, town, fight, therapy, woods, diner, boss), code-written sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish blips for every voice\",\n \"online\":\"AI Hub session protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: each copy plays the same seeded Main Street round and sees the others as ghosts. No other networking.\",\n \"testing\":\"Efficient, lightweight testing: headless Chromium smoke runs, an attract-mode autopilot playing the whole episode, keyboard and fake-gamepad checks, the AI Hub harness (2 and 4 players, host-leave) and a 13-viewport WebKit matrix. No real iOS Safari or physical DualSense.\",\n \"research\":\"None online beyond the engine handoff and AI Hub docs; the Sopranos tone is from memory.\",\n \"environment\":\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n \"model\":\"Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n \"usage\":\"Session time about 35 minutes (18:13 to about 18:48). Cost and token counts: unknown.\"\n}\ntf=[\"About 9 real issues: the attract autopilot's scene changes dropped the demo flag, it snagged on NPCs and lamp posts, it stopped short of exit zones, the woods objective pointed at an unreachable waypoint, a 'move' action warning, em dashes that the font cannot draw, and overlapping HUD, boss-bar and results text. A stale web server also gave a false hub-harness failure.\",\n\"Two were game-breaking for the flow (the woods and yard soft-locks of the attract tour); none crashed, and no JS errors appeared in any run.\",\n\"Running the attract-mode autopilot through the whole episode while polling game state and taking screenshots: it exercised dialogue, combat, scene changes, saves and the ending in one go.\",\n\"The viewport matrix overflow check: it reported all 13 viewports clean, but a full-screen canvas game cannot overflow, so only its screenshots helped. Also my first long run piped through tail, which showed nothing until it finished.\"]\nef=[\"The rigs and lighting give a lot of look for free, and the standard features (pause, settings, controls rebinding, save slots) plus Dialog with live portraits, Combo/Attack and FlowField saved a great deal of work.\",\n\"Yes: input.label has no 'move' action, FlowField ignores prop colliders so the autopilot walked into NPCs, game.go clears state so every scene change had to carry the demo flag, and I guessed a 'ring' prop that does not exist.\",\n\"The game layer: enemy AI, the stress/gut/respect systems, shakedown and therapy scripts, the attract autopilot, AI Hub ghost sync, furniture boxes, and drawn PlayStation/Xbox glyphs (the engine font has no controller symbols).\",\n\"Confirming exact method semantics without reading the engine source, such as what combo.hits expects, overlay coordinates, and how scene changes interact with game state.\",\n\"I would overhaul how area changes work: re-entering the whole scene through game.go, which clears timers and particles, is awkward for rooms within one game.\",\n\"Add first-class solid props and NPC colliders shared by Body and FlowField, and controller glyph shapes in the font.\"]\npf=[\"The clear definition of done and fixed deliverables, the 10-foot controller-first philosophy, the inverted-stick toggle as a realistic constraint, and the instruction to pick the title with a real random generator.\",\n\"Whether the single-file rule and 'dependencies need not be included' conflict, how the bracketed file name should be formatted, what 'root' means, and how a hub round with no title screen fits the standalone title and attract mode.\",\n\"Scope: a complete vertical slice with attract mode, hub ghost play, controller glyphs, saves, a story in the source's tone and only code-written assets.\",\n\"A deterministic full-episode bot test asserting chapter progression, which I approximated with the attract autopilot, plus a run on a real DualSense.\"]\nd={\"sourceInformation\":src,\"testingFeedback\":tf,\"engineFeedback\":ef,\"promptFeedback\":pf,\n\"aiHub\":{\"name\":\"The Soprano Diet\",\"tagline\":\"Ducks. Doctors. Deli meat.\",\"description\":\"A Jersey mob boss tries to survive a day of shakedowns, rival crews, therapy and a dream in the snow while his cardiologist watches his plate. Brawl, bargain and keep your stress down.\",\"type\":\"Game\",\"genre\":\"Action\",\"source\":\"The Sopranos (1999-2007)\",\"series\":\"The Sopranos\",\"players\":\"1–4\",\"controls\":\"Move: left stick/WASD. Punch: Square/J/click. Dodge: Circle/Space. Interact: Cross/E. The Look: Triangle/Q. Eat: L1/R. Camera: R3/V.\",\"tags\":[\"story\",\"comedy\",\"pixel art\",\"retro\",\"boss fights\",\"top-down\"]}}\njson.dump(d,open('exit-interview.json','w'),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.load(open('exit-interview.json')); 